        <div class="moj_tekst">
            <h2>Animating Circular Motion Using p5.js</h2>

            <p>
                This simple animation demonstrates how an object can move along a circular path
                using the JavaScript library <strong>p5.js</strong>. In the center, there is a fixed point,
                and a red circle moves around it along a predefined path.
            </p>

            <p>
                Using the trigonometric functions <code>cos()</code> and <code>sin()</code>, the position of the object is calculated based on an angle
                that increases over time. This achieves continuous circular motion.
            </p>

            <h3>Animation Example:</h3>

            <div class="canvas-wrapper" id="kruzni-canvas">
            </div>

            <p class="mt-4">
                Later we will introduce additional effects, such as a motion trail, multiple objects, and speed control using the keyboard.
                We will also explain the mathematical functions behind this type of animation.
            </p>
